      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2362827158,
          "type": null,
          "body": "This has probably been true since 4aca4dc3192f4cbf17af7a4fb11d8b30f0f77eef. It is more efficient with a singly-linked list to prepend and then reverse, so this seems reasonable. There are other functions that also return file extension lists that ultimately call `add_extensions()` at some point (wtap_get_file_extensions_list, wtap_get_all_capture_file_extensions_list, wtap_get_all_file_extensions_list). All of those are I believe returned in the reverse of the natural ordering, though I don't think they are displayed to the user currently unlike that one.",
