      "title": "wiretap: return file type extensions in listed order",
      "message": "wiretap: return file type extensions in listed order\n\nBecause of the way `wtap_get_file_extension_type_extensions` works,\nthe returned list has the extensions in the reverse order from how they're\nlisted in `file_type_extensions_base`. This reverse order is then shown to the\nuser in the file open dialog.\n\nThis behavior is mildly surprising, so fix it by reversing the list back into\nthe original order. For consistency, also do this in other functions returning\nextension lists.\n",
      "author_name": "Roman Donchenko",
      "author_email": "rdonchen@outlook.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-02-23T19:44:14.000+02:00",
